---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Community & Volunteer Leadership" current="/community-leadership/" description="Community and volunteer leadership experience from Richard J. Allen, including hospital chaplaincy, volunteer operations and communications, emergency-preparedness coordination, mentoring, technology adoption, and disaster-response service.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">Community & Volunteer Leadership</div>
  <h1>Leadership shows up outside the job title, too.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Volunteer service has reinforced the same habits I use professionally: listening carefully, organizing people and information, communicating clearly, mentoring, protecting confidentiality, and helping people through difficult situations.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="skill-transfer" aria-label="Volunteer skills that transfer to professional work">
    <div class="skill-node teal"><span>LISTEN</span><strong>Understand before acting</strong><small>Useful in coaching, customer work, conflict, and change.</small></div>
    <div class="skill-node blue"><span>ORGANIZE</span><strong>Create structure</strong><small>Useful in meetings, logistics, records, and follow-through.</small></div>
    <div class="skill-node gold"><span>SUPPORT</span><strong>Stay calm under pressure</strong><small>Useful in escalations, service, and difficult conversations.</small></div>
    <div class="skill-node violet"><span>COMMUNICATE</span><strong>Make the next step clear</strong><small>Useful in leadership, training, and coordination.</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Service in practice</div><h2>Different settings, consistent leadership habits.</h2></div><p class="section-note">These experiences complement paid management work; they do not replace it.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal">
      <div class="card-icon">CARE</div>
      <h3>Volunteer Chaplain · Salem Health / Salem Hospital</h3>
      <p><strong>2023–2024</strong></p>
      <p>Provided regular volunteer support in a hospital environment, strengthening skills in careful listening, discretion, confidentiality, compassionate communication, and appropriate coordination with staff.</p>
      <p><strong>Transferable strengths:</strong> emotional intelligence, calm communication, confidentiality, service, and supporting people through difficult moments.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card accent-blue">
      <div class="card-icon">ADMIN</div>
      <h3>Volunteer Operations & Communications</h3>
      <p><strong>Long-running community administration · documented examples 2012–2022</strong></p>
      <p>Handled records and recurring reports, calendar and event coordination, audit and administrative follow-through, annual planning and material-order coordination, leadership communications, training/support for other volunteers, service-project logistics, recurring bulletins, shared-facility scheduling, website access and permissions, program-enrollment communications, and community event support. Also refined and handed off an annual cross-group reporting/history process after learning how to gather information more efficiently across multiple teams.</p>
      <p><strong>Transferable strengths:</strong> operations support, records/reporting, scheduling, recurring communications, training, stakeholder coordination, knowledge transfer, service-project logistics, basic website administration, and follow-through.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card accent-gold">
      <div class="card-icon">MENTOR</div>
      <h3>Youth & Community Service</h3>
      <p><strong>Ongoing volunteer involvement</strong></p>
      <p>Participated in mentoring and community-service activities that involved planning, encouragement, teamwork, and helping others take greater ownership.</p>
      <p><strong>Transferable strengths:</strong> coaching, mentoring, planning, trust-building, and developing confidence in others.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card accent-violet">
      <div class="card-icon">SERVE</div>
      <h3>Disaster-Response Service</h3>
      <p><strong>Florida · circa 2020</strong></p>
      <p>Volunteered in hurricane-cleanup work as part of a community recovery effort, contributing practical labor in a demanding environment.</p>
      <p><strong>Transferable strengths:</strong> teamwork, adaptability, service under difficult conditions, and willingness to help where needed.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Selected leadership examples</div><h2>Service that required real coordination.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Specific examples are included only where the underlying record supports the work.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal">
      <div class="card-icon">READY</div>
      <h3>Emergency Preparedness & Communication Continuity</h3>
      <p><strong>Documented examples · 2012, 2018 & 2023</strong></p>
      <p>Preparedness work progressed from proposing a structured way to capture emergency-relevant skills alongside community contact records, to initiating large-format area-map support for preparedness planning, to coordinating a 48-hour communication-readiness exercise with centralized reporting and follow-through.</p>
      <p><strong>Transferable strengths:</strong> continuity planning, information organization, distributed communication, preparedness support, reporting, and follow-through.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="card accent-blue">
      <div class="card-icon">ADOPT</div>
      <h3>Community Technology Adoption</h3>
      <p><strong>2025</strong></p>
      <p>Planned and coordinated a community website-adoption effort, added upcoming event information to the site, worked with other facilitators, and organized a support approach in which younger members could help people less comfortable with the technology.</p>
      <p><strong>Transferable strengths:</strong> change adoption, stakeholder coordination, training planning, hands-on implementation, and user support.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <div class="callout" style="margin-top:1.5rem"><strong>Additional hands-on service:</strong> organized volunteer move-assistance projects and supported public-facing charitable donation events, helping visitors with questions and the donation experience.</div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container">
  <div class="callout"><strong>Professional relevance:</strong> the value here is the pattern—listening, organizing, mentoring, communicating, protecting trust, and helping groups move through real-world needs. Private pastoral details, names of people served, youth identities, household information, and unnecessary religious specifics are intentionally omitted.</div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
